{"explanation":"The exponential function and natural logarithm undo each other: \(\ln(e^x)=x\) and \(e^{\ln x}=x\) for \(x>0\). Their graphs are reflections across the line \(y=x\): each point \((a,e^a)\) on the exponential corresponds to \((e^a,a)\) on the logarithm.","manimCode":"const ax = new Axes({ xRange: [-3, 3, 1], yRange: [-3, 3, 1], xLength: 6, yLength: 6, tips: false });
const expCurve = ax.plot(x => Math.exp(x), { color: BLUE, xRange: [-3, 1.08], numSamples: 350 });
const logCurve = ax.plot(x => Math.log(x), { color: ORANGE, xRange: [0.05, 3], numSamples: 350 });
const mirror = ax.plot(x => x, { color: GRAY, xRange: [-3, 3] });
scene.add(ax, mirror, expCurve, logCurve);
const title = new Text({ text: 'Reflection across y = x', color: WHITE, fontSize: 28 });
title.moveTo([0, 3.25, 0]);
scene.add(title);
const a = new ValueTracker(-1);
const p = new Dot({ point: ax.c2p(-1, Math.exp(-1)), color: BLUE });
const q = new Dot({ point: ax.c2p(Math.exp(-1), -1), color: ORANGE });
p.addUpdater(() => p.moveTo(ax.c2p(a.getValue(), Math.exp(a.getValue()))));
q.addUpdater(() => q.moveTo(ax.c2p(Math.exp(a.getValue()), a.getValue())));
scene.add(p, q);
makeDraggable(p, scene, { onDrag: () => {} });
const controls = new Controls(scene, { position: 'bottom-left', width: 260 });
controls.addSlider({ label: 'x on eˣ', min: -2.5, max: 1, value: -1, step: 0.05, onChange: v => a.setValue(v) });
await scene.wait(999999);"}

